  "query_preview": "..(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 345 AM EDT MON SEP 28 2026\n\nNot too many changes to the forecast for this period. Confidence \nremains high that high pressure centered over the Ohio Valley at the \nstart of the period will continue to keep us dry until Thursday or \nFriday. Confidence is also high that we will be well into the \nwarming trend at the start of the period with highs increasing daily \nuntil the 80s return around Wednesday. The 80s will stick around \nuntil the weekend when highs should start to gradually drop down \ncloser to normal for this time of year. \n\nConfidence remains lower for how our rain chances will evolve late \nnext week into the weekend. Model guidance continues the trend of \nslightly slowing down the onset of PoPs to Friday evening and \npeaking around the Sunday to Monday timeframe. Ensemble \nprobabilties for seeing >.1\" of rain Saturday through Monday \nremain on the higher end at 60-75%. The largest uncertainties at \nthis time remains to be how much rain we could see, where, and \nwhen.",
